<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    What rises off a pilot while the hemogen rush runs, beside the glow on the set's pieces.
    The rush hediff's HediffCompProperties_Effecter names it (HediffDefs/HemogenRush.xml), and
    the pawn's own tick then creates it, ticks it and cleans it up with the hediff
    (PawnStatusEffecters, 1.6 and 1.7), so nothing here is driven or saved by our code.

    Built from flecks that mark no state of a pawn anywhere in the game. Core's Berserk
    effecter, the nearest ready-made look, marks a pawn out of its owner's control wherever it
    appears, and a rushing pilot is under control.

    offsetMode Free: the default measures the pilot's draw position against its cell once, as
    the effecter is created, and keeps that offset for the effecter's life, which misplaces
    every fleck by up to half a cell on a pilot who was walking at that moment. The sprayer
    reads the pilot's draw position each time it spawns (OnSource).

    Sparks: Core's MicroSparks, the embers off a fire, a lightning strike and lava, tinted red,
    from two sprayers. Some come at random in front of the pilot and more on a fixed beat
    behind, where the pilot's own sprite and the random ones in front hide the beat.

    Both:
    - scale 0.5~0.8 is under the 0.8~1.2 the game throws them at off a fire
      (FleckMaker.ThrowMicroSparks), and speed 0.35~0.6 well under its 1.2, so they drift
      about a cell up and do not fly.
    - angle -25~25 with absoluteAngle is up the screen whichever way the pilot faces.
      fleckUsesAngleForVelocity makes the fleck move along it.
    - positionRadius 0.35 scatters them across the warcasket's width.
    - The flecks do not follow the pilot, so a running pilot leaves them behind as a short
      trail.
    - color multiplies the fleck's own, and its shader adds the result to the scene: the
      tint keeps the red and takes out most of the green and blue.

    In front, at random:
    - chancePerTick 0.03 is a roll every tick, 1.8 a second on average with uneven gaps. One
      lasts 1.9 seconds, so three or four show at once.
    - positionOffset raises the origin 0.3 cells from the pilot's center, to the chest of the
      warcasket.

    Behind, on a beat:
    - HPWC_HemogenSparkBehind is the same fleck on the layer under the pilot
      (FleckDefs/HemogenSparkBehind.xml).
    - ticksBetweenMotes 15 is four a second, over twice the random sprayer's 1.8, since the
      pilot's sprite covers the first part of each one's life.
    - No positionOffset: they start around the pilot's center, so the ones that show come out
      from behind the sprite on every side.
  -->
  <EffecterDef>
    <defName>HPWC_HemogenRush</defName>
    <offsetMode>Free</offsetMode>
    <children>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerChance</subEffecterClass>
        <fleckDef>MicroSparks</fleckDef>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <chancePerTick>0.03</chancePerTick>
        <positionOffset>(0, 0, 0.3)</positionOffset>
        <positionRadius>0.35</positionRadius>
        <scale>0.5~0.8</scale>
        <color>(255, 70, 50)</color>
        <absoluteAngle>true</absoluteAngle>
        <fleckUsesAngleForVelocity>true</fleckUsesAngleForVelocity>
        <angle>-25~25</angle>
        <speed>0.35~0.6</speed>
        <rotationRate>-12~12</rotationRate>
      </li>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerContinuous</subEffecterClass>
        <fleckDef>HPWC_HemogenSparkBehind</fleckDef>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <ticksBetweenMotes>15</ticksBetweenMotes>
        <positionRadius>0.35</positionRadius>
        <scale>0.5~0.8</scale>
        <color>(255, 70, 50)</color>
        <absoluteAngle>true</absoluteAngle>
        <fleckUsesAngleForVelocity>true</fleckUsesAngleForVelocity>
        <angle>-25~25</angle>
        <speed>0.35~0.6</speed>
        <rotationRate>-12~12</rotationRate>
      </li>
    </children>
  </EffecterDef>
</Defs>
